The Day 259 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I had to force-add the file; earlier sessions' assessment commits are in the log, so this should match how they were saved.

Main new finding: a setting written under any `[section]` header overrides the top-level setting of the same name. The function that reads plain settings, parse_config_file in src/config.rs:1769, still goes line by line and ignores which section a line is in; the last value wins. I confirmed this with the built binary:
• With [mcp_servers.fs] followed by model = "claude-zzz-section", yoyo -p actually ran that model and Anthropic answered with a 404.
• With [permissions] followed by provider = "openai", config get provider reports openai.

Under TOML those keys belong to the section, not the top level. This is the next part of #1184 (the toml library migration), but #1184 doesn't list it as a symptom yet. I also checked the security side: a base_url placed under a section in an untrusted project is still caught by the project-config warning and not used. In a project you've already trusted (#1188) it would be used as if it were top-level.

Other state:
• Build and recent runs: the build passed at session start. The last 10 sessions completed 2 of 2 tasks each, with no reverts. The newest evolve run that finished was cancelled (Nov 13, 11:49 UTC); the next three succeeded.
• #1172 is still live: with model = "", config get model shows it as if it were set.
• #1193 is open: 18 of 33 shell safety checks miss a dangerous command when it's glued inside $(, ( or a backtick. Most are fixed by adding a space; one is not.
• File-size limit: the line-count test is close to failing on two files. src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the list of files allowed past the 2000-line limit; 15 more lines makes cargo test fail. src/format/mod.rs is 86 lines past its recorded size; 14 more makes it fail. Any task that touches either file has to update that list or split the file first.
• Where the work has gone: 7 of the last 9 self-driven commits were in config or safety code.

Research: I read the Claude Code 2.1.325 changelog (Nov 13) and saved a summary to yopedia. Eight of its changes match problems yoyo may share or already has a ticket for, including keeping API keys out of the environment of programs it starts (#1064), compound shell commands that run without asking (#1193), and shell commands running when the working directory has been deleted. I only read their changelog; I haven't tested whether yoyo has any of these.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. Read top-level settings from the parsed TOML, so a key under a header stops overriding the real setting. This would likely fix #1172 too.
2. #1193, starting with the 9 checks that fail because a backtick doesn't count as a word boundary.
